(I) To the extent that this Part prevents the exclusion or restriction of any liability it also prevents -

(a) the liability or its enforcement subject to restrictive or onerous conditions;

(b) or restricting any right or remedy in of the liability, or subjecting a person to any in consequence of his pursuing any such or remedy;

(c) or restricting rules of evidence or and (to that extent) sections 4, 7, 8and 9 also prevent excluding or restricting liability by reference to terms and notices which or restrict the relevant obligation or duty.

(2) But an agreement in writing to submit present or differences to arbitration is not to be treated under this Part as excluding or restricting any liability.
